  "arithmetic_proofs": [
    "Let d > 1, 0 < n = u32_frames * 1e9 < 2^62, s = max(ceil(log2(d)) - 2, 0), P = 2^(64+s), and m = ceil(P/d). P >= 2^62*d, so 0 <= n*m/P - n/d < n/P < 1/d. Fractions n/d lie on a grid spaced 1/d apart, so this error cannot cross the next integer: floor(n*m/P) = floor(n/d). The product fits u128, and m fits u64. Zero/unit rates and zero frames retain their existing branches.",
    "For reciprocal construction, q = u64::MAX / d and r = u64::MAX % d + 1 give 2^64 = q*d + r, with 0 < r <= d. Therefore ceil(2^(64+s)/d) = (q << s) + ceil((r << s)/d). Here d <= u32::MAX and s <= 30, so r << s fits u64 and the sum is at most 2^63. This replaces u128 division without changing the reciprocal.",
    "For minimum-period rounding, min % fundamental determines padding in [0, fundamental-1]. Adding that padding produces exactly ceil(min/fundamental)*fundamental. A checked addition fails precisely when the old checked product exceeded u32::MAX. Zero and invalid range guards and the final maximum-period test are preserved."
  ],
  "code_simplified": [
    "Remove the frame conversion correction multiply, remainder subtraction, comparison and increment. Use the high product and a right shift instead; pack the u32 divisor and u32 shift into the previous u64 divisor space.",
    "Remove period quotient increment/reconstruction and checked multiplication. Reuse the division remainder to add only the missing padding.",
    "Remove u128 division from reciprocal setup. Compute the identical coefficient with bounded u64 quotient/remainder arithmetic. No production unsafe code was added."
  ],
  "retention_basis": [
    "Frame conversion improves 1.185-1.265x at representative audio rates in its immediate comparison; the final artifact remains faster than the original pass baseline.",
    "Period rounding improves 1.176-1.265x across aligned, rounded, large and overflow fixtures.",
    "Reciprocal setup improves 1.834-2.189x compared with the intermediate wide setup. This recovers the initial roughly eight-cycle setup increase; at 48000 Hz the separately measured original/intermediate/final setup medians are about 72/79/37 cycles.",
    "Converter metadata remains 16 bytes with 8-byte alignment, verified by compiling the exact old/new type definitions. Arithmetic paths retain zero heap churn."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "These are component CPU-throughput microbenchmarks. They do not establish a measurable change in full application startup, audio latency, or complete render callback CPU usage.",
    "The exact reciprocal bound depends on the existing u32 frame-count domain and the 1e9 nanoseconds-per-second scale. Widening that domain requires re-deriving the precision.",
    "Initial standalone profiling samples were not used in the retained comparisons; all committed before/after comparisons run the archived binaries serially in alternating process order.",
    "Windows 7 was compile-checked and exercised through legacy COM mocks, not run on Windows 7 hardware. Nightly emits an unrelated unused windows-core workspace dependency warning from its standard-library build."
  ],
